          "note": "✅ Verified: holistic requirements review\nComputer Science at Pitt is offered through the School of Computing and Information (SCI), not the Swanson School of Engineering. Admissions requirements listed are SCI specific: https://www.sci.pitt.edu.",
          "sourceFile": "database-expansion-agent",
          "confidence": "verified",
          "rawOfficialText": "Home | School of Computing and Information Skip to main content School of Computing and Information Main Navigation About Academics Admissions Research Community Give Student Resources People News Events Open Navigation toggle video playback Transform. Connect. Empower. Innovate. We are guided by our vision: Together transforming lives for a better digital future, from our community to the world. Academics Undergraduate Degrees Our undergraduate curriculum is designed to support the education of students who view computing and information as a means of empowerment. Master's Degrees Our graduate degree programs provide students with the tools to analyze and solve the problems created by technology and to push past technology’s boundaries. Doctoral Degrees Many of the world’s most perplexing issues are advanced by research conducted by our PhD students and their faculty mentors. Empowerment Through Learning Explore the computing, library, and information fields through our various academic departments, programs, and initiatives. SCI Departments and Programs Innovative Research As the field of technology is constantly evolving, our research is supported by organizations like the Defense Advanced Research Projects Agency (DARPA), Google, National Institutes of Health (NIH), National Science Foundation (NSF), and more. Explore Our Research Transform at SCI Prepare for your future by networking with like-minded changemakers: participate in workshops, apply for internships, and develop skills to land the job you've envisioned for yourself. Explore Student Resources Connect With Us Alumni and friends of SCI can connect with us at events, support school initiatives, and more.&nbsp; Alumni and Giving Opportunities Slide 1 Slide 2 Slide 3 Slide 4 News Doris Carson Williams Internship recipient on innovative information science and scholarship Paige Frank, a rising senior at SCI and Stamps Scholar, will use her expertise in information science and technology to help growing organizations and businesses broaden their reach. Pitt’s Collaboration with Dell Technologies, NVIDIA brings innovative AI tech to campus researchers A collaboration between the University of Pittsburgh, Dell Technologies, and NVIDIA is bringing innovative tech to campus, connecting Pitt’s research with industry leaders. As part of Dell's Partner Advisory Board, Pitt was invited to try new AI hardware and explore various research endeavors. SCI Associate Professor Balaji Palanisamy Receives Fulbright U.S. Scholar Award Supported by the Iceland-U.S. Fulbright Commission, the prestigious award permits Dr. Palanisamy to visit Reykjavik University in Iceland, where he will conduct a 5-month long research project on detecting security vulnerabilities in Decentralized Finance (DeFi) Platforms. View All News Events View All Events School of Computing and Information Main Navigation About Academics Admissions Research Community Give Student Resources People News Events Information Sciences Building, Fifth Floor 135 N. Bellefield Avenue Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-383-4396 sciadmit@pitt.edu Submit a Website Change Request Close Navigation About Academics Admissions Research Community Give Student Resources People News Events In Focus SCI At A Glance Resources For: Faculty &amp; Staff Prospective Faculty Prospective Students Alumni Corporate&nbsp;Partners Departments &amp; Programs Computer Science Informatics and Networked Systems Information Culture and&nbsp;Data Stewardship Intelligent Systems Request Info &nbsp; Apply &nbsp;&nbsp; Give Now Information Sciences Building Fifth Floor 135 N. Bellefield Avenue Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-383-4396 sciadmit@pitt.edu Close Search Search",
